Support Ticket Classification using NLP

 Project Overview

This project builds a Machine Learning model to automatically classify customer support tickets into different categories using Natural Language Processing (NLP).

The project demonstrates the complete NLP pipeline, including text preprocessing, feature extraction using TF-IDF, and text classification using Machine Learning algorithms.

 Dataset

- Customer Support Tickets Dataset
- Total Records: 8469
- Features: 17

 Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- NLTK
- Scikit-learn

NLP Pipeline

- Data Loading
- Data Cleaning
- Text Preprocessing
- Tokenization
- Stopword Removal
- Lemmatization
- TF-IDF Vectorization
- Train-Test Split
- Model Training
- Model Evaluation
- Prediction


Machine Learning Models

- Multinomial Naive Bayes
- Logistic Regression


 Results

| Model | Accuracy |
|--------|----------|
| Multinomial Naive Bayes | 18.71% |
| Logistic Regression | 19.83% |

Logistic Regression achieved slightly better performance than Naive Bayes.


Future Improvements

- Use BERT or DistilBERT
- Hyperparameter tuning
- Feature engineering
- More informative ticket descriptions


